      {
        "id": 0,
        "original_id": "dbefca6e-e025-5479-91f9-49a2c038e925",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Languages: Tugurt, Berber languages, Tumzabt, Teggargrent\n- Language families: Zenati Berber, Afroasiatic\n- Writing systems: Libyco-Berber script, Tifinagh\n- Places: Oued Righ, Touggourt, Algeria, Tamacine, Tamellaht, Témacine District, Ouargla Province\n\nFacts:\n- The Berber languages constitute a branch of the Afroasiatic language family.\n- The Berber languages were traditionally written with the ancient Libyco-Berber script, which now exists in the form of Tifinagh.\n- Tugurt, also known as Oued Righ Berber and Temacine Tamazight, is a Zenati Berber variety.\n- Tugurt is spoken in some of the oases of the northeastern Oued Righ region around Touggourt in Algeria.\n- Tugurt is also spoken by some residents of Tamacine.\n- Tugurt is closely related to the nearby Tumzabt (Mozabite) and Teggargrent (Ouargli) languages.\n- Tamellaht is a town in the commune of Tamacine, in Témacine District, Ouargla Province, Algeria.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
      {
        "id": 1,
        "original_id": "136266e9-65d3-56d8-b676-263b8ab9ff0d",
        "text": "Page: Tugurt language. Sentence: The Tugurt language, also known as Oued Righ Berber and Temacine Tamazight, is a Zenati Berber variety spoken in some of the oases of the northeastern Oued Righ region around Touggourt in Algeria.\nPage: Tugurt language. Sentence: It is closely related to the nearby Tumzabt (Mozabite) and Teggargrent (Ouargli) languages.\nPage: Berber languages. Sentence: The Berber languages constitute a branch of the Afroasiatic family.\nPage: Berber languages. Sentence: They were traditionally written with the ancient Libyco-Berber script, which now exists in the form of Tifinagh.\nPage: Tamacine. Sentence: The Tugurt language is spoken by some residents of Tamacine.\nPage: Tamellaht. Sentence: Tamellaht is a town in the commune of Tamacine, in Témacine District, Ouargla Province, Algeria.",
        "type": "DocumentChunk"
